Attribution & influence
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture influenced by:
  - OWASP Agentic Top 10 (2026), OWASP GenAI Security Project
  - OWASP Agent Memory Guard (AMG)

This is an independent implementation. Reused open-source components are
integrated as swappable adapters behind AgentLighthouse interfaces, version- and
hash-pinned. Each reused component's license and attribution is retained here as
it is introduced (MIT requires each component's own copyright and permission
notice to be preserved).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reused open-source components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Runtime dependencies (see uv.lock for exact pinned versions + hashes):
  - cryptography          (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause)   Ed25519 signing/verify
  - pydantic, pydantic-settings  (MIT)                   config enforcement boundary
  - fastapi, starlette    (MIT)                          control-plane API
  - httpx, httpcore       (BSD-3-Clause)                 proxy + MCP HTTP client
  - uvicorn               (BSD-3-Clause)                 ASGI server
  - typer, click          (MIT / BSD-3-Clause)           CLI
  - watchfiles            (MIT)                          config hot-reload
  - pyyaml                (MIT)                          config parsing

Optional runtime dependencies (extras):
  - psycopg[binary]       (LGPL-3.0-or-later)            al-core[postgres]: the
    concurrent-writer evidence mirror. Kept OPTIONAL and imported lazily so a
    default (SQLite) deployment neither installs nor links it; AgentLighthouse
    calls it across the standard DB-API/psycopg interface only.

Dashboard (frontend/, built to static assets; Node is a build toolchain only):
  - react, react-dom      (MIT)                          fleet dashboard UI
  - vite, @vitejs/plugin-react, typescript  (MIT / Apache-2.0)   build toolchain
  - @playwright/test      (Apache-2.0)                   dashboard e2e (dev only)

Reference data:
  - BIP-39 English wordlist (2048 words), from bitcoin/bips bip-0039/english.txt
    (public-domain reference wordlist). Embedded verbatim in
    core/al_core/detect/bip39_words.py for the seed-phrase scanner.

Detection/memory adapters: as of Phase 7, AgentLighthouse ships **dependency-free
baseline scanners** (regex + stdlib heuristics) behind the Scanner interface, so
none of the named engines (LLM Guard, Gitleaks/detect-secrets, Presidio, OWASP
AMG) are vendored or linked today, and none are listed here — an attribution for
code we do not ship would be false. They remain swappable adapters behind the
same interface; each will be added here, with its license, at the moment it is
actually introduced.

